<title>USA: First Central founder Simon steps down.</title>
<headline>First Central founder Simon steps down.</headline>
<dateline>LYNBROOK, N.Y. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Central Financial Corp said on Friday that its founder, Martin Simon, resigned as chairman and chief executive officer and was replaced by Andrew Attivissimo.</p>
<p>Simon, 77, who also is the firm's largest stockholder, will remain with First Central as a consultant and board member, the company said.</p>
<p>Attivissimo had been First Central's president and chief operating officer. He has been with the firm since October 1996.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
